      "text": "Hey! You can never go wrong with a massive cookie. 🍪 Here’s a recipe for a \"Pan-Sized\" giant chocolate chip cookie that’s chewy and delicious! 😋\n\n**Ingredients:**\n*   1/2 cup softened butter\n*   1/2 cup brown sugar\n*   1/4 cup white sugar\n*   1 egg\n*   1 tsp vanilla extract\n*   1 ½ cups flour\n*   ½ tsp baking soda\n*   A pinch of salt\n*   1 cup chocolate chips\n\n**Steps:**\n1.  Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C).\n2.  Cream the butter and sugars together until fluffy. Mix in the egg and vanilla. \n3.  Stir in the flour, baking soda, and salt. Fold in those chocolate chips!\n4.  Press the dough into a greased 9-inch round cake pan.\n5.  Bake for 15–20 minutes until golden. Let it cool before digging in!\n\nNeed a nice spatula to get that giant cookie out, or maybe a recommendation for some gourmet chocolate chips to level it up? I’m here if you need! ✨",
